      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "When you open the SteamVR overlay, it turns down the resolution of the game which is running in the background. When you are going back in to the game you will have a bit of a performance spike, since it now instantly has to render at a way higher resolution.\nThis normally doesn't cause any big problems other than a really short lag when going back in to the game.\nOne question though, are you on Windows 11? If so that's why you have that performance hit for a bit longer. SteamVR has a bit of trouble with Windows 11 atm, sometimes you will get really weird stutters / lags for no reason those will also take a while to go away (if they do at all).",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-05-02T04:12:54.578Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "If you use SteamVr and press the menu on your controller to bring up the overlay to look at your desktop or do anything in the overlay, then go back into vrchat theres a good 50/50 chance that when you return to vrchat you will be greeted with 5 fps. Sometimes it goes away after a few seconds, sometimes it goes away if you open your steamvr overlay again multiple times or sometimes you just have to close steamvr and restart. I don't have anything like OVR or any mods installed which caused issues in the past. Being an avid SoundPad user this makes my life living hell.",
